    <summary>Types clipboard text as keystrokes where paste is blocked: VM consoles, iLO/iDRAC, KVM-over-IP, RDP and paste-blocked fields.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
**The last mile for text that cannot be pasted.**

ClipTyper reads the Windows clipboard on a hotkey (default `Ctrl+Alt+V`) or a floating overlay button and types the text as keystrokes into the active window. It is made for places where `Ctrl+V` does not work: VMware vSphere / VMRC, Proxmox noVNC, Hyper-V, Dell iDRAC, HPE iLO, KVM-over-IP, RDP sessions with clipboard redirection disabled, and paste-blocked password fields.

### Features
- Unicode typing or VK Compatibility Mode with a selectable target keyboard layout (type into a US-layout console from a German PC)
- Floating overlay button for fullscreen RDP / KVM sessions
- Credential Auto-Type for user name and password, optional clipboard auto-clear
- Escape abort, focus-loss protection, configurable delay and newline handling
- Runs in user space, no administrator rights, zero telemetry

### Package notes
- Installs for the current user to `%LocalAppData%\Programs\ClipTyper` (the official non-admin installer) and enables start with Windows; this can be turned off in Settings.
- ClipTyper is not started automatically after a Chocolatey install. Start it from the Start Menu.
- The executable is not code-signed. Release checksums are published with every GitHub release (`SHA256SUMS.txt`).
]]></description>
